{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3211"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of jewellery and related articles"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3211"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :jewellery/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :materials-safety :consumer-protection]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :jewellery-workshop-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "JewelryAdvisor ⊣ Jewellery Workshop Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A jewellery-
 workshop PLANT OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for precious-metal
 casting/setting/polishing lines producing finished jewellery and
 related articles (rings/chains/pendants/bracelets in gold/silver/
 platinum/palladium) -- not direct casting/setting/polishing-line-
 equipment control authority and not a hallmarking/purity-assay
 certification authority. Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Thirteen
 concrete governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD
 invariants: propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed
 proposal-effect allowlist (no direct casting/setting/polishing-line-
 equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block, permanent
 hallmarking/purity-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues a hallmark or purity-assay certification), independent
 workshop-equipment verification/registration before maintenance
 scheduling, independent batch verification/registration before
 shipment coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute
 against the batch's own logged production quantity, double-schedule
 guard, metal-type validation, precious-metal-purity plausibility
 validation, precious-metal-weight plausibility validation, and
 defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 (materials-safety solvent/acid hazard, theft/security concern,
 authenticity concern) ALWAYS escalates to a human workshop supervisor;
 `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
